        "band": "C",
        "rationale": "The command structure is readable and the repository build analyzer reported no findings, but argument validation, exception boundaries, unchecked scanner-result assumptions, and tightly coupled dependencies create several meaningful reliability and testability risks. Test coverage is unknown."
      },
      "summary": "The implementation is generally clear, but it can silently accept invalid scan arguments, allow path-resolution exceptions to escape, fail while formatting otherwise valid scanner output, and is difficult to unit-test without invoking the concrete security scanner.",
