          "ruleId": "built-in:code",
          "aspect": "error-handling",
          "severity": "medium",
          "state": "open",
          "title": "Path normalization can throw outside the command\u0027s error boundary",
          "description": "Path.GetFullPath is evaluated before the try block. Invalid path syntax and other path-resolution failures can therefore escape Run entirely instead of producing the documented CLI-style error message and nonzero return code.",
          "recommendation": "Move path normalization and existence validation inside the try block, and classify expected path-related exceptions as usage errors with exit code 2.",
          "evidence": null,
