          "ruleId": "built-in:code",
          "aspect": "correctness",
          "severity": "medium",
          "state": "open",
          "title": "The scan command silently accepts invalid arguments",
          "description": "Scan parsing searches for --by-level and selects the first non-option token as the path without rejecting unknown options or additional positional arguments. For example, a misspelled flag can be ignored while the command reports success, and \u0060quality scan --help\u0060 performs a scan rather than displaying help.",
          "recommendation": "Use an explicit argument parser for scan, recognizing help and --by-level, accepting at most one path, and returning exit code 2 for every unknown or duplicate argument.",
