          "ruleId": "built-in:code",
          "aspect": "error-handling",
          "severity": "medium",
          "state": "open",
          "title": "Finding rendering assumes every result has a complete location",
          "description": "Output formatting unconditionally indexes Locations[0] and dereferences Range. A scanner result with no locations or a location without a range causes an exception after the summary has already been written, producing partial output and a generic failure exit.",
          "recommendation": "Validate scanner results before rendering or format absent locations safely. If complete locations are a domain invariant, enforce that invariant when findings are constructed and expose a non-null primary location.",
